  "id": "Compound::DB01104 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Sertraline, through its interaction with Clomifene and Irbesartan, appears to exert a modulatory effect on Cyp1a2, a key enzyme in drug metabolism. The evidence suggests that Sertraline may cause the development of Hepatocellular Adenoma or Monoparesis, both of which are linked to Clomifene or Irbesartan, which in turn bind to Cyp1a2. This creates a chain of interactions where Sertraline indirectly influences Cyp1a2 through its effects on the downstream compounds Clomifene and Irbesartan. The lowest common ancestor of these entities is an Organic Amino Compound, suggesting a shared biochemical pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Sertraline could influence Cyp1a2, though the exact nature of this influence remains to be fully elucidated.",
